{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 5,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.5.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.5.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician upon Nehiloth, A Psalm of David. Give ear to my words, O LORD, consider my meditation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.5.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.5.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hearken to the voice of my cry, my King, and my God: for to thee will I pray.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.5.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.5.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My voice shalt thou hear in the morning, O LORD; in the morning will I direct ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my prayer",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to thee, and will look up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.5.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.5.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not a God that hath pleasure in wickedness: neither shall evil dwell with thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.5.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.5.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The foolish shall not stand in thy sight: thou hatest all workers of iniquity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.5.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.5.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt destroy them that speak falsehood: the LORD will abhor the bloody and deceitful man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.5.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.5.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But as for me, I will come ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "into",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy house in the multitude of thy mercy: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in thy fear will I worship towards thy holy temple.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.5.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.5.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lead me, O LORD, in thy righteousness, because of my enemies; make thy way straight before my face.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.5.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.5.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no faithfulness in their mouth; their inward part ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " very wickedness; their throat ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an open sepulcher; they flatter with their tongue.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.5.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.5.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Destroy thou them, O God; let them fall by their own counsels; cast them out in the multitude of their transgressions; for they have rebelled against thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.5.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.5.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But let all those that put their trust in thee rejoice: let them ever shout for joy, because thou defendest them: let them also that love thy name be joyful in thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.5.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.5.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou, LORD, wilt bless the righteous; with favor wilt thou compass him as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a shield.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
